  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on the probability of a favorable outcome and prefers the one with the higher probability. The individual explicitly weighs the probability of a favorable outcome (i.e., not getting 0) and chooses the option with higher certainty (100% vs. 80%), even though it means accepting a lower maximum payout. The individual’s justification centers on avoiding a reduction in probability of a favorable outcome (i.e., not wanting to worsen the 100% chance), which directly aligns with the reason’s rule. The individual’s reasoning is consistent with the decision reason: they prefer the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. Therefore, the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

